a special sunday edition of pftot  everyday weekend style but the nfl never  takes a weekend off especially not with  the season approaching used to be the  nfl got started on labor day weekend now  it's just a few days after the last  unofficial weekend of summer that we'll  have the texans and the chiefs get  together and let's start with the guy  who was once the first overall pick of  the houston texans jadavian clowney  traded last year on labor day weekend to  the seahawks at the time when he was  subject to the franchise tag hadn't  shown up for anything hadn't signed the  tender next thing you know the texans  kick in seven million to get a deal done  he goes to seattle macy's in the  background by the way he goes to seattle  he spends a year there and then he  spends six months almost on the open  market finally agreeing to terms with  the tennessee titans now  it was an interesting saturday night  because even though there was a report  that the deal was done with tennessee  the deal wasn't done with tennessee and  there were efforts made by teams like  the saints and the seahawks to get back  into it and to get clowney to choose  them over tennessee at the end of the  day though he decided to reunite with  mike rabel who was the defensive  coordinator in houston before becoming  the head coach of the tennessee titans  and that relationship presumably went a  long way to get clowney to take an offer  reportedly worth up to 15 million  dollars which means the base value is  less than that we don't know how much  less i had heard last night the talk was  in the range of 12 million dollars what  does he have to do to earn the  difference and the reality is he went  for months  taking the position he would not accept  15 million dollars from anyone with the  season approaching with his agent bus  cook terminated now clowney gets the  deal done to become a member of the  titans and the thing about clowning  don't look at the three and a half sacks  last year look at the film look at the  disruption the f up the play  ability as chris sims calls it although  he'd love to  say something other than f up the play  that's what clowney does he's a  disruptive force other guys get the  tackles the sacks the fumbles the  interceptions it's clowney who can blow  a gaping hole in an offensive line and  destroy a game plan and that's what the  titans will be counting on him to do as  they try to build on  a season that unexpectedly landed them  in the afc championship and maybe with a  guy like clowney if he's healthy maybe  that's the difference if they  get together with the chiefs again in  the post season and remember last year  the titans had a 10-point lead twice in  the first half first they got to get  back to the playoffs clowney will help  them make that happen in a very crowded  and competitive afc south  on saturday a contract we had been  expecting for weeks to sean watson  agreeing to terms with the texans on his  second deal before he was ever in a  position where he was going to take any  hits potentially get injured the injury  risk shifts to the texans with a  four-year extension on top of the two  years that watson had left on his first  round rookie contract from 2017 he gets  paid a lot of money  to compare his contract year by year  through the first four seasons with the  patrick mahomes deal whether it's  signing bonus whether it's money  guaranteed for skill injury and cap at  signing cash flow year one two three  four  all metrics better than the patrick  mahomes deal and after four years  watsonville the contract for two more  seasons  and focusing on as the agents presumably  did doing a deal that compared very  favorably to patrick mahomes there's  some other quarterback contracts you  could look at and say those deals may be  better those quarterbacks got more fully  guaranteed money at signing those  quarterbacks have better cash flow  through one year two year three years  four years one name right off the top of  the head ryan tannahill who has 118  million over four years with his  four-year deal with the titans deshawn  wants to make 110 million over the next  four years which guy would you rather  have over the next four years i'll do  respect to ryan tannehill i doubt that  anyone would say give me tana hill over  watson and yet tannehill over the next  four seasons will make eight million  more than watson and after those four  seasons tannehill will be a free agent  again watson will be under contract for  two more years so  and there are other contracts as well  that  will compare favorably both to watson  and mahomes watson compares favorably to  my homes the reality is the mahomes deal  in the early years is so bad in all due  respect it doesn't take much  to compare favorably to the first few  years of the patrick mahomes contract  but the good news is  watson was able to avoid getting crammed  into that same pigeonhole of a long-term  ultra long-term ridiculous long-term  contract like the deal that my home  signed the chiefs that's going to be a  battle for more quarterbacks to fight as  they try to get their contracts dak  prescott coming up soon others will be  following suit like kyler murray  eventually lamar jackson after this  season when he's eligible for a second  deal it's always better to take a  shorter term contract and have  flexibility  than to to lock yourself in for a dozen  years like patrick mahomes did now i  understand why i did it i get it  it's his right to do it but when we look  across the board at all quarterback  contracts and compare them some are  going to be better than others and the  quarterbacks who commit for 12 years  are going to be in a tough spot to be  able to say i got the best of the  contracts watson's deal  better than mahomes the reality there  are other deals out there better than  both and it makes you wonder how long  until the players realize it and how  long until the market  gets to a point where both watson emma  homes will say i think it's time to redo  those deals because maybe they weren't  as good as they ultimately could have  been  adrian peterson cut abruptly by the  washington football team late last week  quickly finds a new home with the  detroit lions a one-year deal with a  veteran minimum salary worth i'm told up  to 2.3 million based upon yards and  touchdowns and on the surface the lions  have a crowded house in the backfield  they've got carrion johnson second  rounder in 2018 deandre swift second  rounder in 2020 why would they need  adrian peterson well the reality is  johnson has missed 14 games in two  seasons due to injury 14 games nearly  half of his time with the team he hasn't  been able to play and look that's not a  knock on carry on johnson it's a tough  demanding position and adrian peterson  has proven since 2007 far more often  than not he can line up and go deandre  swift had an injury that knocked him out  for a lot of camp and it called into  question his availability for the month  of september so peterson gives them a  guy who can fill in for swift while  swift is getting healthy and also a  hedge against the possibility that  johnson will get injured again  and the end result is you know wherever  adrian peterson goes except new orleans  because it didn't work out there because  they didn't want to use him the way he  wanted to be used he's gotten  opportunities and it feels like he's  going to get opportunities with the  lions and wouldn't be something if he  passes barry sanders on the all-time  rushing list while playing for the  detroit lions oh and by the way he'll  get to play in minnesota again this year  he'll play the vikings twice i'm sure  that he was attracted to that  possibility i'm told two other teams  were interested in adrian peterson but  they wanted to wait  until after week one one of those teams  by the way  plays early in week one and possibly  wears helmets that are  painted red uh other than that i'm not  gonna say anything more about it a  couple of other things to address before  we wrap this up  the buffalo bills working out a new  contract with cornerback trudavius white  remember when he was thinking about  opting out  you'll wonder what was said and done  behind the scenes to get him to commit  to playing and you wonder how much of  the seeds of the contract that was  announced yesterday  were planted back in late july early  august as white was deciding whether or  not to play and look perfectly  legitimate for a player to use the  possibility of opting out as a tool to  get what he deserves white wanted a  second contract he's gotten his second  contract before the season begins and  it's a good deal for him it's a good  deal for the bills he's a great young  defensive back we haven't seen all the  details yet of the tridevious white deal  but the bottom line is he signed it he's  happy the team's happy and now the bills  go forward with a key piece of their  defense in place for years to come  the la chargers have had keenan allen  under contract for multiple years and  they will have him under contract for  multiple years still to come third  contract for keenan allen reportedly  the second highest paid receiver in the  nfl now we know the devil's always in  the details with deals like this we'll  we'll get into the nooks and crannies  when the full numbers become available  and see where keenan allen really fits  in the overall receiver salary hierarchy  but if he truly is the second highest  paid receiver in the nfl there may be  some other receivers who look at that  and say  pay me  possibly with a profanity thrown in on  the front end like they did in the movie  goodfellas but you know the reality is  keenan allen been around for a while not  currently one of the upper echelon  receivers in the nfl and i know he  probably would take exception to that  but look  every receiver worth his salt should  take exception to that the reality is  there can only be so many of the best of  the best receivers in the nfl and most  people would say allen currently isn't  in that group if he's being paid like  he's in that group it's only going to  make other guys want to get paid even  more money than what they're already  making so a busy weekend in the nfl we  may have another edition of pftot by the  time it's all said and done who knows  what's going to happen sunday who knows  what's going to happen monday but what i  do know is thursday night it will be the  texans and the chiefs on nbc and then  just a few days after that the full  slate of week one games  culminating in sunday night with the  cowboys and the rams getting together  for the first game ever at the new  stadium in englewood that's it for now  we'll be talking to you soon check us  out around the clock at  profootballtalk.com  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

